I can’t produce this table or heatmap reliably from the available Human Protein Atlas tools.

The required analysis depends on the HPA immune-cell single-cell dataset, specifically:

- the complete sets of genes annotated **“lineage enriched” in NK-cells alone** and **“lineage enriched” in B-cells alone**;
- nTPM values for those genes in **NK-cells, naive B-cells, memory B-cells, and T-regs**;
- expression values across **all immune-cell types**;
- the complete set of all lineage-enriched genes to define the overlap-test universe.

The available tools can retrieve individual-protein information and general tissue, brain, blood, and subcellular-expression data, but they do not expose the required immune single-cell lineage-enrichment tables or nTPM matrix. Therefore, I cannot determine the cohort sizes, cohort means, top-ten genes, heatmap values, or an exact overlap test without estimating or importing data outside the available HPA interface.

The HPA search results do confirm several NK-associated CD-marker proteins—for example **KLRK1/CD314, KLRC1/CD159a, KLRB1/CD161, KLRC2/CD159c, CD160, NCAM1/CD56, KLRD1/CD94, NCR3/CD337, CD226, CD244, FCGR3A/CD16, CD300A, and SLAMF6/CD352**—but this is not equivalent to identifying which of them belong to the requested NK-only lineage-enriched cohort.

